        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Back pain in humans can be reduced by using a transcutaneous electrical nerve stimulation (TENS) machine.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 14
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A TENS machine uses electrical impulses to stimulate nerve endings near the site of the pain.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 14
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It is thought that TENS triggers the release of natural painkillers called endorphins at synapses.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 14
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fig. 5.2 shows synapses in a pain pathway.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 14
            }
          },
